2025-08-27 11:15:05,681 INFO pdf-ingest Refreshing profile object after commit id=efc4e515-4e86-403c-8fe1-a08420c15187 (obj={'_sa_instance_state': <sqlalchemy.orm.state.InstanceState object at 0xffff9fb66cf0>, 'id': UUID('efc4e515-4e86-403c-8fe1-a08420c15187'), 'email': 'email@email.com', 'skills': ['Investigation skills', 'Safety compliance', 'Criminal justice knowledge', 'Restraining devices', 'Martial arts/Physical combat', 'training'], 'raw_text': "ROBERT COOPER\n\nSECURITY GUARD\n\nLOS ANGELES, CA 90291, UNITED STATES\n\n3868683442\n\nDETAILS\n\nPROFILE\n\n1515 Pacific Ave\nLos Angeles, CA 90291\nUnited States\n3868683442\nemail@email.com\n\nPlace of birth\nSan Antonio\n\nDriving license\nFull\n\nLINKS\n\nLinkedIn\n\nPinterest\n\nResume Templates\n\nBuild this template\n\nSKILLS\n\nInvestigation skills\n\nSafety compliance\n\nCriminal justice knowledge\n\nRestraining devices\n\nMartial arts/Physical combat \ntraining\n\nHOBBIES\n\nRunning, Mtb, Enduro\n\nLANGUAGES\n\nEnglish\n\nSpanish\n\nItalian\n\nSafety conscious, attentive Security Guard with eight years experience in protecting and \nguarding VIP individuals in the military and defense sectors. Proficient at observing \nsurroundings and immediate settings for possible threats of nonhuman and human nature. \nPresently finishing a bachelor’s in criminal justice and qualified as a CPO (Certified \nProtection Guard).\xa0\n\nEMPLOYMENT HISTORY\n\nSecurity Guard at ADT Security, Port Washington\nJanuary 2021 — April 2022\n\nResponsible for completing reports by recording information, observations, occurrences, \nand surveillance activities, including interviewing of witnesses and acquiring signatures.\n\n• Maintaining environments by monitoring the grounds and equipment controls.\n• Logging into security headquarters on the hour during the day and every 2 hours \n\nwith the night shift, notifying control of all in order statuses.\n\n• Utilizing armed force when necessary, to protect company belongings, visitors, \n\nemployees, and clients when needed.\xa0\n\n• Apprehending suspects in the event of security breaches and detaining them until \n\nthe police arrive on the scene.\n\nSecurity Guard at Copwatch, Jogbani\nJanuary 2020 — April 2022\n\nPrimary purpose is to scan area of grounds for objects/ items that seem out of place and \nnotifying Center management of bags or packages that are unattended.\n\nInspecting restrooms after closing time for vagrants/ unauthorized personnel. \xa0\n\n•\n• Monitoring selected areas via CCTV app on smart devices.\n• Ensure flawless equipment operation by finishing preventive maintenance \n\nnecessities, reading the manufacturer's instructions, troubleshooting \nmalfunctions, organizing for repairs if needed, and assessing new equipment and \ntechniques\n\nEDUCATION\n\nCertified Protection Guard Program (CPOP), International Foundation for Protection \nGuards, Alexandria\nJanuary 2021 — April 2022\n\nSecurity Guard Certificate Program (SOCP), ASIS International, North Naples\nApril 2022 — April 2022\n\n• Course Curriculum: Law Enforcement Ethics, Foundations in Criminal Law, Report \n\nWriting, Criminal Profiling, Interviewing Techniques, Crisis Intervention.\n\nS.A.F.E. Approach Level II Training, Hawaii Western College\nJanuary 2015 — November 2019\n\n\x0cACHIEVEMENTS\n\n• Decreased theft of hotel items like linen, towels, décor pieces, and cutlery by 73% \n\nby improving vigilance strategies, particularly for guests leaving the hotel.\n• Enhancing detection/monitoring procedures by having 15 360 degrees CCTV \n\n•\n\n•\n\ncameras installed at the back of shopping aisles and in storerooms, which cut \nproduct stock theft by 93%.\nIntroduced inventive loss prevention techniques by installing an X-ray scanning \nsystem at every entrance and exit in the building, which reduced theft by 28%.\nImproved access control, which reduced unauthorized entry and solicitation by \n26% using an announcement notification app, where visitors may be admitted/ \ndeclined entry straight from the employee’s smart device.\n\n\x0c", 'confidence': 0.7500000000000001, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2025, 8, 27, 11, 10, 12, 29524, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'summary': '1515 Pacific Ave\nLos Angeles, CA 90291\nUnited States\n3868683442\nemail@email.com', 'name': 'United States', 'experience': None, 'meta': {'llm': 'mistral', 'source': 'server_parse', 'ai_flags': [], 'filename': 'cv.pdf', 'parsedAt': 1756293305646, 'education': [{'school': None, 'degree': None, 'fieldOfStudy': None, 'startDate': None, 'endDate': None, 'description': 'Running Mtb Enduro'}, {'school': 'Safety conscious', 'degree': 'attentive Security Guard with eight years experience in protecting and guarding VIP individuals in the military and defense sectors. Proficient at observing surroundings and immediate settings for possible threats of nonhuman and human nature. Presently finishing a bachelor’s in criminal justice and qualified as a CPO (Certified Protection Guard).', 'fieldOfStudy': None, 'startDate': None, 'endDate': None, 'description': None}, {'school': 'EMPLOYMENT HISTORY', 'degree': None, 'fieldOfStudy': None, 'startDate': None, 'endDate': None, 'description': None}, {'school': 'Security Guard at ADT Security', 'degree': None, 'fieldOfStudy': None, 'startDate': None, 'endDate': None, 'description': 'Port Washington January 2021 April 2022'}, {'school': 'Responsible for completing reports by recording information', 'degree': None, 'fieldOfStudy': None, 'startDate': None, 'endDate': None, 'description': 'observations occurrences and surveillance activities including interviewing of witnesses and acquiring signatures.'}, {'school': '• Maintaining environments by monitoring the grounds and equipment controls. • Logging into security headquarters on the hour during the day and every 2 hours', 'degree': None, 'fieldOfStudy': None, 'startDate': None, 'endDate': None, 'description': None}, {'school': 'with the night shift', 'degree': None, 'fieldOfStudy': None, 'startDate': None, 'endDate': None, 'description': 'notifying control of all in order statuses.'}, {'school': '• Utilizing armed force when necessary', 'degree': None, 'fieldOfStudy': None, 'startDate': None, 'endDate': None, 'description': 'to protect company belongings visitors'}, {'school': '• Apprehending suspects in the event of security breaches and detaining them until', 'degree': None, 'fieldOfStudy': None, 'startDate': None, 'endDate': None, 'description': None}, {'school': 'the police arrive on the scene.', 'degree': None, 'fieldOfStudy': None, 'startDate': None, 'endDate': None, 'description': None}], 'llmRefined': True, 'mistral_url': 'https://api.mistral.ai/v1/chat/completions', 'achievements': ['Decreased theft of hotel items like linen, towels, décor pieces, and cutlery by 73%', 'Enhancing detection/monitoring procedures by having 15 360 degrees CCTV', 'cameras installed at the back of shopping aisles and in storerooms, which cut', 'product stock theft by 93%.', 'system at every entrance and exit in the building, which reduced theft by 28%.', 'Improved access control, which reduced unauthorized entry and solicitation by', '26% using an announcement notification app, where visitors may be admitted/'], 'llmRefinedAt': None, 'llmConfidence': 0.5, 'payload_shape': ['model', 'messages', 'temperature', 'max_tokens'], 'mistral_attempts': 1}, 'version': 1})
